            <ArticleTitle>Stent deformation at the edge of a high pressure balloon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>508-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2015.03.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(15)00065-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Focal ultrashort balloons are essential tools for lesion preparation and final stent expansion. However, they may cause a major distortion of the adjacent segments. Here we report a case with a stent deformation emphasizing the importance of utilizing intravascular imaging techniques for optimal interventions.</AbstractText>
